---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="AI-assisted Security Review">
  <h1>AI-assisted security review</h1>
  <p>
    Separate from code review on a pull request, this is the automated layer that watches the
    <em>supply chain</em> continuously:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dependabot</strong> — alerts can identify vulnerable dependencies; eligible security updates can propose fixes when enabled. The outdated <code>marked@0.3.19</code> seed exists only in historical baseline <code>05cdada</code>, not this safe version.</li>
    <li><strong>Dependency review</strong> — can be configured as a required PR check; it is not included in this rehearsal's build workflow.</li>
    <li><strong>Secret scanning with push protection</strong> — can flag supported secret patterns and block pushes. Detection of the historical fake placeholder was not verified, and the placeholder has been removed from this safe version.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Upgrading Marked addresses known dependency advisories, not all XSS. Marked does not sanitize
    HTML. This feedback widget also sanitizes rendered Markdown with DOMPurify and constructs
    name and timestamp text without inserting user-provided HTML.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where Copilot Code Review looks at a diff, this layer looks at the whole dependency graph and
    commit history — the exact surface OWASP's A03: Software Supply Chain Failures is about.
  </p>
</Layout>
